  "lineage": "Tunisian malouf classical Andalusi-Arabic art-music tradition, the Tunisian recension of the broader Maghrebi-Andalusi nuba descended from medieval al-Andalus through the post-1492 expulsion-diaspora settlement (with Testour as a principal Andalusi-refugee settlement). The Tunisian repertoire comprises thirteen canonical nubat. The early-twentieth-century Rachidia Institute (Tunis, 1934) consolidated the canon. Performance integrates male choir-and-soloist with oud, rebab, qanun, nay, and darbuka. Distinguished from Moroccan al-Āla by Tunisian-specific suite-cycle and Rachidia-Institute-canonized repertoire.",
